import SsspFlow.PlanarMap

/-!
# Splitting a rotation system at a set of corners

This is the topological core of splitting a planar map at a connected set of corners into planar
disks and of replacing those disks. Everything here is about permutations and genus, with no drawing
and no Jordan curve argument. As in `SsspFlow.PlanarMap`, a dart `d` also names the corner between
`d` and `rot d`.

## First returns

For `f : Equiv.Perm D` and `S : Finset D`, `firstReturn f S` sends `x ∈ S` to `f^[k] x`, with `k`
the least positive integer such that `f^[k] x ∈ S`, and fixes every point outside `S`
(`firstReturn_spec`, `firstReturn_of_not_mem`). `FixesOff ν S` says that `ν` fixes every point
outside `S`. `Trail` is the first point of `S` on a forward orbit, as an inductive relation.

* (F1) `fconnect_firstReturn_iff`: on `S`, the first return connects the same points as `f`.
* (F2) `firstReturn_mul_right`, `firstReturn_mul_left`: for `FixesOff ν S`,
  `firstReturn (f * ν) S = firstReturn f S * ν` and `firstReturn (ν * f) S = ν * firstReturn f S`.
* (F3) `firstReturn_firstReturn`: for `T ⊆ S`, `firstReturn (firstReturn f S) T = firstReturn f T`.
* (F4) `orb_add_card_compl`: `orb f + card Sᶜ = miss f S + orb (firstReturn f S)`, where `orb`
  counts orbits and `miss f S` counts the orbits of `f` disjoint from `S`. The orbits missing `S` do
  not change under `ν` (`miss_mul_right`, `miss_mul_left`), which gives the counts `orb_mul_right`
  and `orb_mul_left`.

## Skeleton and split

For `R : RotSystem D` and `Γ : Finset D`, put `a := R.nodeReturn Γ`, `b := R.faceReturn Γ` and
`ψ := R.psi Γ = a * b`. `R.skeleton Γ` is the hypermap `permMap a b` on `D`, with node `a`, face `b`
and edge `(a * b)⁻¹`; every dart outside `Γ` is a fixed point of all three. `R.SkeletonConnected Γ`
says that any two elements of `Γ` lie in one component of it, and by `gcomp_skeleton_iff` this is
the connectivity of the graph on `Γ` that joins corners at one vertex or on one face.

`R.glue ν` has the same reversal and the rotation `rot * ν`, and `R.split Γ` is `R.glue a⁻¹`. Its
rotation closes each sector on itself, and its vertices are the sectors. Its first returns to `Γ`
are `1` and `ψ` (`nodeReturn_split`, `faceReturn_split`). `split_split` says that splitting at
`Γ₁ ⊆ Γ₂` and then at `Γ₂` is splitting at `Γ₂`, and `glue_split` that gluing the split with `a`
gives back `R`.

* The identity. `genus_split` holds for every `Γ`, with `P := R.split Γ` and all counts on `D`:
  `g(R) + C(P) + Cˢ = g(P) + g(skeleton) + C(R) + orb ψ`.
* The tiles. `gcomp_split_iff`: the components of `P` are the classes of the equivalence relation
  generated by `v = rev u` and `u ∉ Γ ∧ v = rot u` (`TileLink`).
* The disks. `split_planar`: for planar connected `R` and nonempty connected `Γ`, the split and the
  skeleton are planar, every component of the split meets `Γ`, and two elements of `Γ` lie in one
  component of the split exactly if `ψ` connects them. So there is exactly one `ψ`-orbit per
  component (`numComponents_split`).

## Replacement

`IsDisks` collects what a replacement needs: a planar map with marked corners `Γ'`, at most one per
vertex, at least one per component, and exactly one orbit of `ψ' := P'.faceReturn Γ'` per component.
`split_isDisks` says that a split has this form.

* `glue_planar`: for `P'` with `IsDisks` and `ν'` fixing the complement of `Γ'`, if the skeleton
  `permMap ν' (ν'⁻¹ * ψ')` is connected on `Γ'` and planar, then `P'.glue ν'` is planar and
  connected with first returns `ν'` and `ν'⁻¹ * ψ'`.
* `glue_planar_of_conjVia`, `replace_planar`: for a planar connected `R`, nonempty connected `Γ`,
  and a bijection `β : Γ' ≃ Γ` that carries `ψ'` to `ψ` (`ConjVia`), the map `R.replace Γ P' β`,
  which is `P'` glued along the transport of `a`, is planar and connected, with the transports of
  `a` and `b` as first returns. The skeleton does not change, since the genus of `permMap a b`
  depends only on its action on the marked corners (`permMap_genus_eq`). `split_replace` says that
  the split of a replacement is the map of disks, and `replace_split` that replacing the components
  of a split by themselves gives back `R`.

## An instance

`triangleCorners` is a set of two corners of `triangle`, at one vertex and on one face. It satisfies
the hypotheses of `split_planar` (`triangle_split_planar`), the split has exactly two tiles there
(`triangle_split_two_tiles`), and it consists of disks (`triangle_replace`).

Not here: an embedding in the plane or a drawing of the disks, since `Planar` is the property of the
hypermap; a concrete replacement on other darts, beyond `replace_split`.
-/

set_option autoImplicit false

namespace SsspFlow

open FourColor

section FirstReturn

variable {D : Type*} [Fintype D] [DecidableEq D]

/-! ### Permutations that fix the complement of a set -/

/-- `ν` fixes every point outside `S`. -/
def FixesOff (ν : Equiv.Perm D) (S : Finset D) : Prop := ∀ x, x ∉ S → ν x = x

namespace FixesOff

variable {ν μ : Equiv.Perm D} {S T : Finset D}

omit [Fintype D] [DecidableEq D] in
theorem mem_iff (h : FixesOff ν S) (x : D) : ν x ∈ S ↔ x ∈ S := by
  constructor
  · intro hx
    by_contra hn
    rw [h x hn] at hx
    exact hn hx
  · intro hx
    by_contra hn
    have hxx : ν x = x := ν.injective (h _ hn)
    rw [hxx] at hn
    exact hn hx

omit [Fintype D] [DecidableEq D] in
theorem one (S : Finset D) : FixesOff (1 : Equiv.Perm D) S := fun _ _ => rfl

omit [Fintype D] [DecidableEq D] in
theorem inv (h : FixesOff ν S) : FixesOff ν⁻¹ S := fun x hx =>
  Equiv.Perm.inv_eq_iff_eq.2 (h x hx).symm

omit [Fintype D] [DecidableEq D] in
theorem mul (h : FixesOff ν S) (h' : FixesOff μ S) : FixesOff (ν * μ) S := fun x hx => by
  rw [Equiv.Perm.mul_apply, h' x hx, h x hx]

omit [Fintype D] [DecidableEq D] in
theorem mono (h : FixesOff ν S) (hST : S ⊆ T) : FixesOff ν T := fun x hx =>
  h x fun hs => hx (hST hs)

end FixesOff

/-! ### The first return -/

omit [DecidableEq D] in
/-- A point of `S` returns to `S`. -/
theorem exists_return (f : Equiv.Perm D) {S : Finset D} {x : D} (hx : x ∈ S) :
    ∃ k, 0 < k ∧ (⇑f)^[k] x ∈ S := by
  obtain ⟨k, hk, h⟩ := exists_iterate_eq_self f.injective x
  exact ⟨k, hk, by rw [h]; exact hx⟩

/-- The function behind `firstReturn`. -/
private def firstReturnFun (f : Equiv.Perm D) (S : Finset D) (x : D) : D :=
  if hx : x ∈ S then (⇑f)^[Nat.find (exists_return f hx)] x else x

private theorem firstReturnFun_spec (f : Equiv.Perm D) (S : Finset D) {x : D} (hx : x ∈ S) :
    ∃ k, 0 < k ∧ firstReturnFun f S x = (⇑f)^[k] x ∧ (⇑f)^[k] x ∈ S ∧
      ∀ j, 0 < j → j < k → (⇑f)^[j] x ∉ S := by
  have hs := Nat.find_spec (exists_return f hx)
  refine ⟨_, hs.1, ?_, hs.2, fun j hj hjk hm => Nat.find_min (exists_return f hx) hjk ⟨hj, hm⟩⟩
  simp [firstReturnFun, hx]

private theorem firstReturnFun_of_not_mem (f : Equiv.Perm D) (S : Finset D) {x : D} (hx : x ∉ S) :
    firstReturnFun f S x = x := by
  simp [firstReturnFun, hx]

omit [Fintype D] [DecidableEq D] in
private theorem return_injective_aux {f : Equiv.Perm D} {S : Finset D} {x y : D} {k l : ℕ}
    (hk : 0 < k) (hx : x ∈ S) (hl : ∀ j, 0 < j → j < l → (⇑f)^[j] y ∉ S) (hkl : k ≤ l)
    (h : (⇑f)^[k] x = (⇑f)^[l] y) : x = y := by
  obtain ⟨m, rfl⟩ := Nat.exists_eq_add_of_le hkl
  rw [Function.iterate_add_apply] at h
  have hxy : x = (⇑f)^[m] y := (f.injective.iterate k) h
  rcases Nat.eq_zero_or_pos m with rfl | hm
  · exact hxy
  · exact absurd (hxy ▸ hx) (hl m hm (by omega))

private theorem firstReturnFun_injective (f : Equiv.Perm D) (S : Finset D) :
    Function.Injective (firstReturnFun f S) := by
  intro x y hxy
  by_cases hx : x ∈ S <;> by_cases hy : y ∈ S
  · obtain ⟨k, hk, hkx, -, hkm⟩ := firstReturnFun_spec f S hx
    obtain ⟨l, hl, hly, -, hlm⟩ := firstReturnFun_spec f S hy
    rw [hkx, hly] at hxy
    rcases le_total k l with h | h
    · exact return_injective_aux hk hx hlm h hxy
    · exact (return_injective_aux hl hy hkm h hxy.symm).symm
  · obtain ⟨k, -, hkx, hkS, -⟩ := firstReturnFun_spec f S hx
    rw [hkx, firstReturnFun_of_not_mem f S hy] at hxy
    exact absurd (hxy ▸ hkS) hy
  · obtain ⟨l, -, hly, hlS, -⟩ := firstReturnFun_spec f S hy
    rw [hly, firstReturnFun_of_not_mem f S hx] at hxy
    exact absurd (hxy ▸ hlS) hx
  · rwa [firstReturnFun_of_not_mem f S hx, firstReturnFun_of_not_mem f S hy] at hxy

/-- The first return of `f` to `S`: it sends `x ∈ S` to `f^[k] x`, with `k` the least positive
integer such that `f^[k] x ∈ S`, and it fixes every point outside `S`. -/
noncomputable def firstReturn (f : Equiv.Perm D) (S : Finset D) : Equiv.Perm D :=
  Equiv.ofBijective (firstReturnFun f S)
    (Finite.injective_iff_bijective.1 (firstReturnFun_injective f S))

theorem firstReturn_of_not_mem (f : Equiv.Perm D) {S : Finset D} {x : D} (hx : x ∉ S) :
    firstReturn f S x = x :=
  firstReturnFun_of_not_mem f S hx

/-- The specification of the first return on `S`. -/
theorem firstReturn_spec (f : Equiv.Perm D) {S : Finset D} {x : D} (hx : x ∈ S) :
    ∃ k, 0 < k ∧ firstReturn f S x = (⇑f)^[k] x ∧ (⇑f)^[k] x ∈ S ∧
      ∀ j, 0 < j → j < k → (⇑f)^[j] x ∉ S :=
  firstReturnFun_spec f S hx

theorem fixesOff_firstReturn (f : Equiv.Perm D) (S : Finset D) : FixesOff (firstReturn f S) S :=
  fun _ hx => firstReturn_of_not_mem f hx

theorem firstReturn_mem_iff (f : Equiv.Perm D) (S : Finset D) (x : D) :
    firstReturn f S x ∈ S ↔ x ∈ S :=
  (fixesOff_firstReturn f S).mem_iff x

/-! ### Trails

The first point of `S` on the forward orbit of a dart, as an inductive relation. All statements
about the first return reduce to it. -/

/-- `Trail f S y z`: `z` is the first point of `S` on the forward orbit of `y`, `y` included. -/
inductive Trail (f : Equiv.Perm D) (S : Finset D) : D → D → Prop
  | here {y : D} : y ∈ S → Trail f S y y
  | step {y z : D} : y ∉ S → Trail f S (f y) z → Trail f S y z

namespace Trail

variable {f g ν : Equiv.Perm D} {S T : Finset D} {y z z' : D}

omit [Fintype D] [DecidableEq D] in
theorem mem (h : Trail f S y z) : z ∈ S := by
  induction h with
  | here hy => exact hy
  | step _ _ ih => exact ih

omit [Fintype D] [DecidableEq D] in
theorem unique (h : Trail f S y z) (h' : Trail f S y z') : z = z' := by
  induction h generalizing z' with
  | here hy =>
    cases h' with
    | here _ => rfl
    | step hn _ => exact absurd hy hn
  | step hn _ ih =>
    cases h' with
    | here hy => exact absurd hy hn
    | step _ ht => exact ih ht

omit [Fintype D] [DecidableEq D] in
theorem to_fconnect (h : Trail f S y z) : fconnect f y z := by
  induction h with
  | here _ => exact connect_refl _
  | step _ _ ih => exact connect_trans (fconnect1 f _) ih

omit [Fintype D] [DecidableEq D] in
theorem congr (hfg : ∀ w, w ∉ S → g w = f w) (h : Trail f S y z) : Trail g S y z := by
  induction h with
  | here hy => exact Trail.here hy
  | step hn _ ih => exact Trail.step hn (by rw [hfg _ hn]; exact ih)

omit [Fintype D] [DecidableEq D] in
theorem mul_left (hν : FixesOff ν S) (h : Trail f S y z) : Trail (ν * f) S (ν y) (ν z) := by
  induction h with
  | here hy => exact Trail.here ((hν.mem_iff _).2 hy)
  | step hn _ ih =>
    rw [hν _ hn]
    exact Trail.step hn ih

end Trail

omit [Fintype D] [DecidableEq D] in
theorem trail_of_iterate (f : Equiv.Perm D) (S : Finset D) {y : D} {n : ℕ}
    (hn : (⇑f)^[n] y ∈ S) (hj : ∀ j, j < n → (⇑f)^[j] y ∉ S) :
    Trail f S y ((⇑f)^[n] y) := by
  induction n generalizing y with
  | zero => exact Trail.here hn
  | succ n ih =>
    rw [Function.iterate_succ_apply] at hn ⊢
    refine Trail.step (hj 0 (Nat.succ_pos n)) (ih hn fun j hjn => ?_)
    have h := hj (j + 1) (Nat.succ_lt_succ hjn)
    rwa [Function.iterate_succ_apply] at h

theorem firstReturn_trail (f : Equiv.Perm D) {S : Finset D} {x : D} (hx : x ∈ S) :
    Trail f S (f x) (firstReturn f S x) := by
  obtain ⟨k, hk, hkx, hkS, hkj⟩ := firstReturn_spec f hx
  obtain ⟨m, rfl⟩ : ∃ m, k = m + 1 := ⟨k - 1, by omega⟩
  rw [hkx, Function.iterate_succ_apply]
  rw [Function.iterate_succ_apply] at hkS
  refine trail_of_iterate f S hkS fun j hj => ?_
  have h := hkj (j + 1) (Nat.succ_pos j) (by omega)
  rwa [Function.iterate_succ_apply] at h

theorem firstReturn_eq_of_trail (f : Equiv.Perm D) {S : Finset D} {x z : D} (hx : x ∈ S)
    (h : Trail f S (f x) z) : firstReturn f S x = z :=
  (firstReturn_trail f hx).unique h

theorem fconnect_firstReturn (f : Equiv.Perm D) (S : Finset D) (x : D) :
    fconnect f x (firstReturn f S x) := by
  by_cases hx : x ∈ S
  · exact connect_trans (fconnect1 f x) (firstReturn_trail f hx).to_fconnect
  · rw [firstReturn_of_not_mem f hx]

/-! ### (F1) The first return has the orbits of `f` on `S` -/

theorem fconnect_of_fconnect_firstReturn {f : Equiv.Perm D} {S : Finset D} {x y : D}
    (h : fconnect (firstReturn f S) x y) : fconnect f x y :=
  connect_sub (fun a _ hab => hab ▸ fconnect_firstReturn f S a) h

private theorem fconnect_firstReturn_of_trail {f : Equiv.Perm D} {S : Finset D} {w z : D}
    (h : fconnect f w z) (hz : z ∈ S) :
    ∀ {u : D}, Trail f S w u → fconnect (firstReturn f S) u z := by
  induction h using Relation.ReflTransGen.head_induction_on with
  | refl =>
    intro u ht
    rw [ht.unique (Trail.here hz)]
  | @head a c hac _ ih =>
    obtain rfl : f a = c := hac
    intro u ht
    cases ht with
    | here ha => exact connect_trans (connect_of_rel rfl) (ih (firstReturn_trail f ha))
    | step _ ht' => exact ih ht'

/-- **(F1)** For `x, y ∈ S`, the first return connects `x` and `y` exactly if `f` does. -/
theorem fconnect_firstReturn_iff (f : Equiv.Perm D) {S : Finset D} {x y : D} (hx : x ∈ S)
    (hy : y ∈ S) : fconnect (firstReturn f S) x y ↔ fconnect f x y :=
  ⟨fconnect_of_fconnect_firstReturn, fun h => fconnect_firstReturn_of_trail h hy (Trail.here hx)⟩

/-! ### (F2) Multiplying by a permutation that fixes the complement -/

/-- **(F2)**, right side. -/
theorem firstReturn_mul_right (f : Equiv.Perm D) {ν : Equiv.Perm D} {S : Finset D}
    (hν : FixesOff ν S) : firstReturn (f * ν) S = firstReturn f S * ν := by
  ext x
  rw [Equiv.Perm.mul_apply]
  by_cases hx : x ∈ S
  · refine firstReturn_eq_of_trail _ hx ?_
    rw [Equiv.Perm.mul_apply]
    exact (firstReturn_trail f ((hν.mem_iff x).2 hx)).congr fun w hw => by
      rw [Equiv.Perm.mul_apply, hν w hw]
  · rw [firstReturn_of_not_mem _ hx, hν x hx, firstReturn_of_not_mem _ hx]

/-- **(F2)**, left side. -/
theorem firstReturn_mul_left (f : Equiv.Perm D) {ν : Equiv.Perm D} {S : Finset D}
    (hν : FixesOff ν S) : firstReturn (ν * f) S = ν * firstReturn f S := by
  ext x
  rw [Equiv.Perm.mul_apply]
  by_cases hx : x ∈ S
  · exact firstReturn_eq_of_trail _ hx ((firstReturn_trail f hx).mul_left hν)
  · rw [firstReturn_of_not_mem _ hx, firstReturn_of_not_mem _ hx, hν x hx]

/-! ### (F3) First returns compose -/

private theorem trail_firstReturn {f : Equiv.Perm D} {S T : Finset D} (hTS : T ⊆ S) {y z : D}
    (h : Trail f T y z) : ∀ {w : D}, Trail f S y w → Trail (firstReturn f S) T w z := by
  induction h with
  | @here y hy =>
    intro w hw
    rw [hw.unique (Trail.here (hTS hy))]
    exact Trail.here hy
  | @step y z hn _ ih =>
    intro w hw
    cases hw with
    | here hyS => exact Trail.step hn (ih (firstReturn_trail f hyS))
    | step _ ht => exact ih ht

/-- **(F3)** The first return to `T` of the first return to `S ⊇ T` is the first return to `T`. -/
theorem firstReturn_firstReturn (f : Equiv.Perm D) {S T : Finset D} (hTS : T ⊆ S) :
    firstReturn (firstReturn f S) T = firstReturn f T := by
  ext x
  by_cases hx : x ∈ T
  · exact firstReturn_eq_of_trail _ hx
      (trail_firstReturn hTS (firstReturn_trail f hx) (firstReturn_trail f (hTS hx)))
  · rw [firstReturn_of_not_mem _ hx, firstReturn_of_not_mem _ hx]

/-! ### Counting components -/

omit [Fintype D] [DecidableEq D] in
private theorem eq_of_connect_of_fixed {e : D → D → Prop} {S : Set D}
    (hfix : ∀ x y, x ∉ S → e x y → y = x) {x y : D} (hx : x ∉ S) (h : connect e x y) : y = x := by
  induction h with
  | refl => rfl
  | @tail b c _ hbc ih => exact (hfix b c (by rw [ih]; exact hx) hbc).trans ih

/-- If no link leaves a point outside `S`, the points outside `S` are components of their own. -/
theorem nComp_univ_eq {e : D → D → Prop} (hs : ConnectSym e) (S : Finset D)
    (hfix : ∀ x y, x ∉ S → e x y → y = x) :
    nComp e Set.univ = nComp e (S : Set D) + Sᶜ.card := by
  have hc : Closed e ((S : Set D)ᶜ) := Closed.of_forward hs fun x y hxy hx => by
    rw [hfix x y hx hxy]
    exact hx
  have hc' : Closed e (S : Set D) := by simpa using hc.compl
  rw [nComp_compl hc']
  congr 1
  have hinj : Set.InjOn (comp e) ((S : Set D)ᶜ) := fun x hx y _ hxy =>
    (eq_of_connect_of_fixed (S := (S : Set D)) (fun a b ha hab => hfix a b ha hab) hx
      ((comp_eq_iff hs).1 hxy)).symm
  rw [nComp, hinj.ncard_image, ← Finset.coe_compl, Set.ncard_coe_finset]

omit [Fintype D] [DecidableEq D] in
/-- The components meeting a set are the components meeting its closure. -/
theorem nComp_closure {e : D → D → Prop} (hs : ConnectSym e) (a : Set D) :
    nComp e (FourColor.closure e a) = nComp e a := by
  unfold nComp
  congr 1
  apply Set.Subset.antisymm
  · rintro _ ⟨x, ⟨y, hy, hxy⟩, rfl⟩
    exact ⟨y, hy, ((comp_eq_iff hs).2 hxy).symm⟩
  · exact Set.image_mono (subset_closure a)

omit [Fintype D] [DecidableEq D] in
/-- If every point is connected to a point of `s`, all components meet `s`. -/
theorem nComp_univ_of_meets {e : D → D → Prop} (hs : ConnectSym e) {s : Set D}
    (h : ∀ x, ∃ y ∈ s, connect e x y) : nComp e Set.univ = nComp e s := by
  unfold nComp
  congr 1
  apply Set.Subset.antisymm
  · rintro _ ⟨x, -, rfl⟩
    obtain ⟨y, hy, hxy⟩ := h x
    exact ⟨y, hy, ((comp_eq_iff hs).2 hxy).symm⟩
  · exact Set.image_mono (Set.subset_univ s)

omit [Fintype D] [DecidableEq D] in
/-- If any two points of a nonempty set are connected, the set meets one component. -/
theorem nComp_eq_one_of_connect {e : D → D → Prop} (hs : ConnectSym e) {s : Set D}
    (hne : s.Nonempty) (h : ∀ x ∈ s, ∀ y ∈ s, connect e x y) : nComp e s = 1 := by
  obtain ⟨x0, hx0⟩ := hne
  rw [nComp, Set.ncard_eq_one]
  refine ⟨comp e x0, Set.ext fun c => ?_⟩
  simp only [Set.mem_image, Set.mem_singleton_iff]
  constructor
  · rintro ⟨x, hx, rfl⟩
    exact (comp_eq_iff hs).2 (h x hx x0 hx0)
  · rintro rfl
    exact ⟨x0, hx0, rfl⟩

/-- A component of `e'` as a set: the points reached from a set by `e'`. -/
private def coarsen (e' : D → D → Prop) (c : Set D) : Set D := {y | ∃ x ∈ c, connect e' x y}

omit [Fintype D] [DecidableEq D] in
private theorem coarsen_comp {e e' : D → D → Prop} (h : ∀ x y, connect e x y → connect e' x y)
    (x : D) : coarsen e' (comp e x) = comp e' x := by
  ext z
  constructor
  · rintro ⟨w, hw, hwz⟩
    exact connect_trans (h _ _ hw) hwz
  · intro hz
    exact ⟨x, connect_refl x, hz⟩

omit [Fintype D] [DecidableEq D] in
private theorem image_comp_eq {e e' : D → D → Prop} (h : ∀ x y, connect e x y → connect e' x y)
    (s : Set D) : comp e' '' s = coarsen e' '' (comp e '' s) := by
  rw [Set.image_image]
  exact Set.image_congr fun x _ => (coarsen_comp h x).symm

omit [DecidableEq D] in
/-- A coarser relation has at most as many components. -/
theorem nComp_le_of_imp {e e' : D → D → Prop} (h : ∀ x y, connect e x y → connect e' x y)
    (s : Set D) : nComp e' s ≤ nComp e s := by
  unfold nComp
  rw [image_comp_eq h s]
  exact Set.ncard_image_le (Set.toFinite _)

omit [DecidableEq D] in
/-- If a coarser relation has as many components on `s`, it connects the same points of `s`. -/
theorem connect_of_nComp_eq {e e' : D → D → Prop} (hs : ConnectSym e) (hs' : ConnectSym e')
    (h : ∀ x y, connect e x y → connect e' x y) {s : Set D} (heq : nComp e' s = nComp e s)
    {x y : D} (hx : x ∈ s) (hy : y ∈ s) (hxy : connect e' x y) : connect e x y := by
  have hinj : Set.InjOn (coarsen e') (comp e '' s) := by
    refine Set.injOn_of_ncard_image_eq ?_ (Set.toFinite _)
    rw [← image_comp_eq h s]
    exact heq
  have hc : comp e x = comp e y := hinj ⟨x, hx, rfl⟩ ⟨y, hy, rfl⟩ (by
    rw [coarsen_comp h, coarsen_comp h, comp_eq_iff hs']
    exact hxy)
  exact (comp_eq_iff hs).1 hc

/-! ### (F4) The count of orbits -/

/-- The number of orbits of a permutation. -/
noncomputable def orb (g : Equiv.Perm D) : ℕ := fcard g Set.univ

theorem orb_eq_add_card {g : Equiv.Perm D} {S : Finset D} (h : FixesOff g S) :
    orb g = fcard g (S : Set D) + Sᶜ.card :=
  nComp_univ_eq (fconnect_sym g.injective) S fun x y hx hxy => by
    rw [← (show g x = y from hxy)]
    exact h x hx

theorem orb_one : orb (1 : Equiv.Perm D) = Fintype.card D := by
  have h := orb_eq_add_card (FixesOff.one (∅ : Finset D))
  simpa using h

omit [Fintype D] [DecidableEq D] in
theorem orb_inv [Finite D] (g : Equiv.Perm D) : orb g⁻¹ = orb g :=
  nComp_congr (fun _ _ => fconnect_inverse (f := ⇑g) (g := ⇑g⁻¹)
    g.symm_apply_apply g.apply_symm_apply) _

/-- The number of orbits of `f` disjoint from `S`. -/
noncomputable def miss (f : Equiv.Perm D) (S : Finset D) : ℕ :=
  fcard f (fclosure f (S : Set D))ᶜ

/-- **(F4)** The orbits of the first return are the orbits of `f` that meet `S` and one fixed point
for every point outside `S`. -/
theorem orb_add_card_compl (f : Equiv.Perm D) (S : Finset D) :
    orb f + Sᶜ.card = miss f S + orb (firstReturn f S) := by
  have hs := fconnect_sym f.injective
  have hs' := fconnect_sym (firstReturn f S).injective
  have h1 : orb f = fcard f (fclosure f (S : Set D)) + miss f S :=
    nComp_compl (closure_closed hs _)
  have h2 : fcard f (fclosure f (S : Set D)) = fcard f (S : Set D) := nComp_closure hs _
  have h3 : fcard f (S : Set D) = fcard (firstReturn f S) (S : Set D) :=
    ncard_image_eq_of_ker _ _ fun x hx y hy => by
      rw [comp_eq_iff hs, comp_eq_iff hs']
      exact (fconnect_firstReturn_iff f hx hy).symm
  have h4 := orb_eq_add_card (fixesOff_firstReturn f S)
  omega

omit [Fintype D] [DecidableEq D] in
private theorem not_mem_fclosure_step [Finite D] (f : Equiv.Perm D) (a : Set D) {x : D}
    (hx : x ∉ fclosure f a) : f x ∉ fclosure f a :=
  fun h => hx ((closure_closed (fconnect_sym f.injective) a x (f x) rfl).2 h)

omit [Fintype D] [DecidableEq D] in
private theorem not_mem_fclosure_of_agree [Finite D] {f g : Equiv.Perm D} {a : Set D}
    (hfg : ∀ x, x ∉ fclosure f a → g x = f x) (x : D) (hx : x ∉ fclosure f a) :
    x ∉ fclosure g a := by
  rintro ⟨y, hy, hxy⟩
  have key : y ∈ (fclosure f a)ᶜ := by
    refine mem_of_connect_of_forward ?_ hxy hx
    rintro u _ rfl hu
    rw [hfg u hu]
    exact not_mem_fclosure_step f a hu
  exact key (subset_closure a hy)

omit [Fintype D] [DecidableEq D] in
private theorem fconnect_of_agree [Finite D] {f g : Equiv.Perm D} {a : Set D}
    (hfg : ∀ x, x ∉ fclosure f a → g x = f x) {x y : D} (hx : x ∉ fclosure f a)
    (h : fconnect f x y) : fconnect g x y := by
  have key : y ∉ fclosure f a ∧ fconnect g x y := by
    induction h with
    | refl => exact ⟨hx, connect_refl _⟩
    | @tail b c _ hbc ih =>
      obtain rfl : f b = c := hbc
      exact ⟨not_mem_fclosure_step f a ih.1, connect_trans ih.2 (connect_of_rel (hfg b ih.1))⟩
  exact key.2

omit [Fintype D] [DecidableEq D] in
/-- Two permutations that agree on the orbits missing `S` miss `S` with as many orbits. -/
theorem miss_eq_of_agree [Finite D] {f g : Equiv.Perm D} {S : Finset D}
    (hfg : ∀ x, x ∉ fclosure f (S : Set D) → g x = f x)
    (hgf : ∀ x, x ∉ fclosure g (S : Set D) → f x = g x) : miss g S = miss f S := by
  have hset : (fclosure g (S : Set D))ᶜ = (fclosure f (S : Set D))ᶜ := Set.ext fun x =>
    ⟨not_mem_fclosure_of_agree hgf x, not_mem_fclosure_of_agree hfg x⟩
  unfold miss
  rw [hset]
  refine ncard_image_eq_of_ker _ _ fun x hx y _ => ?_
  rw [comp_eq_iff (fconnect_sym g.injective), comp_eq_iff (fconnect_sym f.injective)]
  exact ⟨fconnect_of_agree hgf (not_mem_fclosure_of_agree hfg x hx), fconnect_of_agree hfg hx⟩

omit [Fintype D] [DecidableEq D] in
theorem miss_mul_right [Finite D] (f : Equiv.Perm D) {ν : Equiv.Perm D} {S : Finset D}
    (hν : FixesOff ν S) : miss (f * ν) S = miss f S :=
  miss_eq_of_agree
    (fun x hx => by rw [Equiv.Perm.mul_apply, hν x fun h => hx (subset_closure _ h)])
    (fun x hx => by rw [Equiv.Perm.mul_apply, hν x fun h => hx (subset_closure _ h)])

omit [Fintype D] [DecidableEq D] in
theorem miss_mul_left [Finite D] (f : Equiv.Perm D) {ν : Equiv.Perm D} {S : Finset D}
    (hν : FixesOff ν S) : miss (ν * f) S = miss f S :=
  miss_eq_of_agree
    (fun x hx => by
      have h : f x ∉ S := fun h => not_mem_fclosure_step f _ hx (subset_closure _ h)
      rw [Equiv.Perm.mul_apply, hν _ h])
    (fun x hx => by
      have h : (ν * f) x ∉ S := fun h =>
        not_mem_fclosure_step (ν * f) _ hx (subset_closure _ h)
      have h' : f x ∉ S := fun hm => h ((hν.mem_iff _).2 hm)
      rw [Equiv.Perm.mul_apply, hν _ h'])

/-- **(F4)**, right side: the orbits missing `S` cancel. -/
theorem orb_mul_right (f : Equiv.Perm D) {ν : Equiv.Perm D} {S : Finset D} (hν : FixesOff ν S) :
    orb (f * ν) + orb (firstReturn f S) = orb f + orb (firstReturn f S * ν) := by
  have h1 := orb_add_card_compl f S
  have h2 := orb_add_card_compl (f * ν) S
  rw [firstReturn_mul_right f hν, miss_mul_right f hν] at h2
  omega

/-- **(F4)**, left side: the orbits missing `S` cancel. -/
theorem orb_mul_left (f : Equiv.Perm D) {ν : Equiv.Perm D} {S : Finset D} (hν : FixesOff ν S) :
    orb (ν * f) + orb (firstReturn f S) = orb f + orb (ν * firstReturn f S) := by
  have h1 := orb_add_card_compl f S
  have h2 := orb_add_card_compl (ν * f) S
  rw [firstReturn_mul_left f hν, miss_mul_left f hν] at h2
  omega

/-! ### The hypermap of two permutations -/

/-- The hypermap with `node := a`, `face := b` and `edge := (a * b)⁻¹`, the last being forced by
`edgeK`. -/
def permMap (a b : Equiv.Perm D) : Hypermap D where
  edge := ⇑(a * b)⁻¹
  node := ⇑a
  face := ⇑b
  edgeK x := (a * b).apply_symm_apply x

omit [Fintype D] [DecidableEq D] in
private theorem permMap_fixed {a b : Equiv.Perm D} {S : Finset D} (ha : FixesOff a S)
    (hb : FixesOff b S) {x y : D} (hx : x ∉ S) (h : (permMap a b).glink x y) : y = x := by
  rcases h with rfl | rfl | rfl
  · exact (ha.mul hb).inv x hx
  · exact ha x hx
  · exact hb x hx

/-- Outside `S`, every dart of `permMap a b` is a component of its own. -/
theorem permMap_nComp {a b : Equiv.Perm D} {S : Finset D} (ha : FixesOff a S)
    (hb : FixesOff b S) :
    nComp (permMap a b).glink Set.univ = nComp (permMap a b).glink (S : Set D) + Sᶜ.card :=
  nComp_univ_eq (permMap a b).glinkC S fun _ _ hx h => permMap_fixed ha hb hx h

/-- The genus of `permMap a b` depends only on what happens on `S`: outside `S`, a dart contributes
two to the component count, one to the dart count, and three to the orbit counts. -/
theorem permMap_genus_on {a b : Equiv.Perm D} {S : Finset D} (ha : FixesOff a S)
    (hb : FixesOff b S) :
    2 * (permMap a b).genus + fcard (a * b) (S : Set D) + fcard a (S : Set D) +
        fcard b (S : Set D) =
      2 * nComp (permMap a b).glink (S : Set D) + S.card := by
  have h := (permMap a b).evenGenus
  unfold Hypermap.EvenGenus Hypermap.eulerLhs Hypermap.eulerRhs at h
  have hC := permMap_nComp ha hb
  have hE : fcard (permMap a b).edge Set.univ = fcard (a * b) (S : Set D) + Sᶜ.card :=
    (orb_inv (a * b)).trans (orb_eq_add_card (ha.mul hb))
  have hN : fcard (permMap a b).node Set.univ = fcard a (S : Set D) + Sᶜ.card :=
    orb_eq_add_card ha
  have hF : fcard (permMap a b).face Set.univ = fcard b (S : Set D) + Sᶜ.card :=
    orb_eq_add_card hb
  have hD := Finset.card_add_card_compl S
  omega

end FirstReturn

/-! ### Transport along a bijection of marked corners -/

section Transport

variable {D : Type*} [Fintype D] [DecidableEq D] {D' : Type*} [Fintype D'] [DecidableEq D']
  {Γ : Finset D} {Γ' : Finset D'}

/-- `x'` and `x` are matched by the bijection `β`. -/
def Corr (β : Γ' ≃ Γ) (x' : D') (x : D) : Prop := ∃ h : x' ∈ Γ', (β ⟨x', h⟩ : D) = x

omit [Fintype D] [DecidableEq D] [Fintype D'] [DecidableEq D'] in
theorem corr_coe (β : Γ' ≃ Γ) (x : Γ') : Corr β x (β x) := ⟨x.2, rfl⟩

namespace Corr

variable {β : Γ' ≃ Γ} {x' y' : D'} {x y : D}

omit [Fintype D] [DecidableEq D] [Fintype D'] [DecidableEq D'] in
theorem symm (h : Corr β x' x) : Corr β.symm x x' := by
  obtain ⟨hx', rfl⟩ := h
  exact ⟨(β ⟨x', hx'⟩).2, by simp⟩

omit [Fintype D] [DecidableEq D] [Fintype D'] [DecidableEq D'] in
theorem right_unique (h : Corr β x' x) (h' : Corr β x' y) : x = y := by
  obtain ⟨_, rfl⟩ := h
  obtain ⟨_, rfl⟩ := h'
  rfl

omit [Fintype D] [DecidableEq D] [Fintype D'] [DecidableEq D'] in
theorem left_unique (h : Corr β x' x) (h' : Corr β y' x) : x' = y' := by
  obtain ⟨hx, e⟩ := h
  obtain ⟨hy, e'⟩ := h'
  have h1 : (⟨x', hx⟩ : Γ') = ⟨y', hy⟩ := β.injective (Subtype.ext (e.trans e'.symm))
  exact congrArg Subtype.val h1

end Corr

/-- `g'` acts on `Γ'` as `g` acts on `Γ`, through `β`. -/
def ConjVia (β : Γ' ≃ Γ) (g' : Equiv.Perm D') (g : Equiv.Perm D) : Prop :=
  ∀ x' x, Corr β x' x → Corr β (g' x') (g x)

namespace ConjVia

variable {β : Γ' ≃ Γ} {g' h' : Equiv.Perm D'} {g h : Equiv.Perm D}

omit [Fintype D] [DecidableEq D] [Fintype D'] [DecidableEq D'] in
theorem one : ConjVia β (1 : Equiv.Perm D') (1 : Equiv.Perm D) := fun _ _ c => c

omit [Fintype D] [DecidableEq D] [Fintype D'] [DecidableEq D'] in
theorem mul (hg : ConjVia β g' g) (hh : ConjVia β h' h) : ConjVia β (g' * h') (g * h) :=
  fun _ _ c => hg _ _ (hh _ _ c)

omit [Fintype D] [DecidableEq D] [Fintype D'] [DecidableEq D'] in
theorem symm (hg : ConjVia β g' g) : ConjVia β.symm g g' :=
  fun _ _ c => (hg _ _ c.symm).symm

omit [Fintype D] [DecidableEq D] [Fintype D'] [DecidableEq D'] in
theorem pow (hg : ConjVia β g' g) (n : ℕ) : ConjVia β (g' ^ n) (g ^ n) := by
  induction n with
  | zero => simpa using ConjVia.one
  | succ n ih =>
    rw [pow_succ, pow_succ]
    exact ih.mul hg

omit [DecidableEq D] [DecidableEq D'] in
theorem inv (hg : ConjVia β g' g) : ConjVia β g'⁻¹ g⁻¹ := by
  have hn : 0 < orderOf g' * orderOf g := Nat.mul_pos (orderOf_pos g') (orderOf_pos g)
  have h1 : g' ^ (orderOf g' * orderOf g) = 1 := by
    rw [pow_mul, pow_orderOf_eq_one, one_pow]
  have h2 : g ^ (orderOf g' * orderOf g) = 1 := by
    rw [mul_comm, pow_mul, pow_orderOf_eq_one, one_pow]
  have h3 : g'⁻¹ = g' ^ (orderOf g' * orderOf g - 1) :=
    inv_eq_of_mul_eq_one_right (by rw [← pow_succ', Nat.sub_add_cancel hn, h1])
  have h4 : g⁻¹ = g ^ (orderOf g' * orderOf g - 1) :=
    inv_eq_of_mul_eq_one_right (by rw [← pow_succ', Nat.sub_add_cancel hn, h2])
  rw [h3, h4]
  exact hg.pow _

end ConjVia

omit [Fintype D] [DecidableEq D] [Fintype D'] [DecidableEq D'] in
private theorem exists_connect_corr {e' : D' → D' → Prop} {e : D → D → Prop} {β : Γ' ≃ Γ}
    (hf : ∀ x' x y', Corr β x' x → e' x' y' → ∃ y, Corr β y' y ∧ e x y)
    {x' y' : D'} {x : D} (hxy : connect e' x' y') (hx : Corr β x' x) :
    ∃ y, Corr β y' y ∧ connect e x y := by
  induction hxy with
  | refl => exact ⟨x, hx, connect_refl x⟩
  | tail _ hbc ih =>
    obtain ⟨z, hz, hxz⟩ := ih
    obtain ⟨w, hw, hzw⟩ := hf _ _ _ hz hbc
    exact ⟨w, hw, connect_trans hxz (connect_of_rel hzw)⟩

omit [Fintype D] [DecidableEq D] [Fintype D'] [DecidableEq D'] in
/-- Connection is carried along a relation that matches the links. -/
theorem connect_corr {e' : D' → D' → Prop} {e : D → D → Prop} {β : Γ' ≃ Γ}
    (hf : ∀ x' x y', Corr β x' x → e' x' y' → ∃ y, Corr β y' y ∧ e x y)
    {x' y' : D'} {x y : D} (hxy : connect e' x' y') (hx : Corr β x' x) (hy : Corr β y' y) :
    connect e x y := by
  obtain ⟨z, hz, hxz⟩ := exists_connect_corr hf hxy hx
  rwa [hy.right_unique hz]

omit [Fintype D] [DecidableEq D] [Fintype D'] [DecidableEq D'] in
theorem fconnect_corr {β : Γ' ≃ Γ} {g' : Equiv.Perm D'} {g : Equiv.Perm D} (h : ConjVia β g' g)
    {x' y' : D'} {x y : D} (hx : Corr β x' x) (hy : Corr β y' y) (hxy : fconnect g' x' y') :
    fconnect g x y := by
  refine connect_corr ?_ hxy hx hy
  rintro a' a _ hc rfl
  exact ⟨g a, h _ _ hc, rfl⟩

omit [Fintype D] [DecidableEq D] [Fintype D'] [DecidableEq D'] in
/-- Corresponding sets meet as many corresponding components. -/
theorem nComp_corr {e' : D' → D' → Prop} {e : D → D → Prop} (hs' : ConnectSym e')
    (hs : ConnectSym e) (β : Γ' ≃ Γ)
    (hk : ∀ x' x y' y, Corr β x' x → Corr β y' y → (connect e' x' y' ↔ connect e x y)) :
    nComp e' (Γ' : Set D') = nComp e (Γ : Set D) := by
  have h1 : comp e' '' (Γ' : Set D') = (fun x : Γ' => comp e' (x : D')) '' Set.univ := by
    ext c
    constructor
    · rintro ⟨x, hx, rfl⟩
      exact ⟨⟨x, hx⟩, trivial, rfl⟩
    · rintro ⟨x, -, rfl⟩
      exact ⟨x, x.2, rfl⟩
  have h2 : comp e '' (Γ : Set D) = (fun x : Γ' => comp e (β x : D)) '' Set.univ := by
    ext c
    constructor
    · rintro ⟨x, hx, rfl⟩
      exact ⟨β.symm ⟨x, hx⟩, trivial, by simp⟩
    · rintro ⟨x, -, rfl⟩
      exact ⟨_, (β x).2, rfl⟩
  unfold nComp
  rw [h1, h2]
  refine ncard_image_eq_of_ker _ _ fun x _ y _ => ?_
  show comp e' (x : D') = comp e' (y : D') ↔ comp e (β x : D) = comp e (β y : D)
  rw [comp_eq_iff hs', comp_eq_iff hs]
  exact hk _ _ _ _ (corr_coe β x) (corr_coe β y)

omit [Fintype D] [DecidableEq D] [Fintype D'] [DecidableEq D'] in
theorem fcard_corr [Finite D] [Finite D'] {β : Γ' ≃ Γ} {g' : Equiv.Perm D'} {g : Equiv.Perm D}
    (h : ConjVia β g' g) : fcard g' (Γ' : Set D') = fcard g (Γ : Set D) :=
  nComp_corr (fconnect_sym g'.injective) (fconnect_sym g.injective) β fun _ _ _ _ hx hy =>
    ⟨fconnect_corr h hx hy, fconnect_corr h.symm hx.symm hy.symm⟩

omit [DecidableEq D] [DecidableEq D'] in
private theorem permMap_glink_corr {β : Γ' ≃ Γ} {a' b' : Equiv.Perm D'} {a b : Equiv.Perm D}
    (ha : ConjVia β a' a) (hb : ConjVia β b' b) :
    ∀ x' x y', Corr β x' x → (permMap a' b').glink x' y' →
      ∃ y, Corr β y' y ∧ (permMap a b).glink x y := by
  rintro x' x _ hc (rfl | rfl | rfl)
  · exact ⟨_, (ha.mul hb).inv _ _ hc, Or.inl rfl⟩
  · exact ⟨_, ha _ _ hc, Or.inr (Or.inl rfl)⟩
  · exact ⟨_, hb _ _ hc, Or.inr (Or.inr rfl)⟩

omit [DecidableEq D] [DecidableEq D'] in
/-- Matching permutations give matching components. -/
theorem permMap_gcomp_corr {β : Γ' ≃ Γ} {a' b' : Equiv.Perm D'} {a b : Equiv.Perm D}
    (ha : ConjVia β a' a) (hb : ConjVia β b' b) {x' y' : D'} {x y : D} (hx : Corr β x' x)
    (hy : Corr β y' y) : (permMap a' b').gcomp x' y' ↔ (permMap a b).gcomp x y :=
  ⟨fun h => connect_corr (permMap_glink_corr ha hb) h hx hy,
    fun h => connect_corr (permMap_glink_corr ha.symm hb.symm) h hx.symm hy.symm⟩

/-- Matching permutations give the same genus: the genus does not see the darts outside the
marked corners. -/
theorem permMap_genus_eq {a' b' : Equiv.Perm D'} {a b : Equiv.Perm D} (β : Γ' ≃ Γ)
    (ha' : FixesOff a' Γ') (hb' : FixesOff b' Γ') (ha : FixesOff a Γ) (hb : FixesOff b Γ)
    (hca : ConjVia β a' a) (hcb : ConjVia β b' b) :
    (permMap a' b').genus = (permMap a b).genus := by
  have h' := permMap_genus_on ha' hb'
  have h := permMap_genus_on ha hb
  rw [fcard_corr (hca.mul hcb), fcard_corr hca, fcard_corr hcb,
    nComp_corr (permMap a' b').glinkC (permMap a b).glinkC β
      (fun _ _ _ _ hx hy => permMap_gcomp_corr hca hcb hx hy),
    Finset.card_eq_of_equiv β] at h'
  omega

/-- The permutation of `D'` that acts on `Γ'` as `g` acts on `Γ`, through `β`, and fixes the
rest. -/
def transport (β : Γ' ≃ Γ) (g : Equiv.Perm D) (hg : ∀ x, g x ∈ Γ ↔ x ∈ Γ) : Equiv.Perm D' :=
  Equiv.Perm.ofSubtype (β.symm.permCongr (g.subtypePerm hg))

omit [Fintype D] [Fintype D'] [DecidableEq D] in
theorem fixesOff_transport (β : Γ' ≃ Γ) (g : Equiv.Perm D) (hg : ∀ x, g x ∈ Γ ↔ x ∈ Γ) :
    FixesOff (transport β g hg) Γ' :=
  fun _ hx => Equiv.Perm.ofSubtype_apply_of_not_mem _ hx

omit [Fintype D] [Fintype D'] [DecidableEq D] in
theorem conjVia_transport (β : Γ' ≃ Γ) (g : Equiv.Perm D) (hg : ∀ x, g x ∈ Γ ↔ x ∈ Γ) :
    ConjVia β (transport β g hg) g := by
  rintro x' _ ⟨hx', rfl⟩
  have h1 : transport β g hg x' = (β.symm ⟨g (β ⟨x', hx'⟩), (hg _).2 (β ⟨x', hx'⟩).2⟩ : D') :=
    Equiv.Perm.ofSubtype_apply_of_mem _ hx'
  rw [h1]
  exact (show Corr β.symm _ _ from ⟨(hg _).2 (β ⟨x', hx'⟩).2, rfl⟩).symm

omit [Fintype D] [Fintype D'] [DecidableEq D] in
/-- A permutation that fixes the complement of `Γ'` and matches `g` is the transport of `g`. -/
theorem eq_transport {β : Γ' ≃ Γ} {g' : Equiv.Perm D'} {g : Equiv.Perm D}
    (hg : ∀ x, g x ∈ Γ ↔ x ∈ Γ) (hf : FixesOff g' Γ') (hc : ConjVia β g' g) :
    g' = transport β g hg := by
  ext x'
  by_cases hx : x' ∈ Γ'
  · have c : Corr β x' _ := ⟨hx, rfl⟩
    exact (hc _ _ c).left_unique (conjVia_transport β g hg _ _ c)
  · rw [hf x' hx, fixesOff_transport β g hg x' hx]

omit [Fintype D] [DecidableEq D] in
/-- Every permutation that preserves `Γ` matches itself under the identity of `Γ`. -/
theorem conjVia_refl {g : Equiv.Perm D} (hg : ∀ x, g x ∈ Γ ↔ x ∈ Γ) :
    ConjVia (Equiv.refl Γ) g g := by
  rintro x _ ⟨hx, rfl⟩
  exact ⟨(hg x).2 hx, rfl⟩

end Transport

namespace RotSystem

variable {D : Type*} [Fintype D] [DecidableEq D] (R : RotSystem D)

/-! ### The skeleton -/

/-- `a`: the first return of the rotation to `Γ`. -/
noncomputable def nodeReturn (Γ : Finset D) : Equiv.Perm D := firstReturn R.rot Γ

/-- `b`: the first return of the face permutation to `Γ`. -/
noncomputable def faceReturn (Γ : Finset D) : Equiv.Perm D := firstReturn R.facePerm Γ

/-- `ψ := a * b`. -/
noncomputable def psi (Γ : Finset D) : Equiv.Perm D := R.nodeReturn Γ * R.faceReturn Γ

theorem fixesOff_nodeReturn (Γ : Finset D) : FixesOff (R.nodeReturn Γ) Γ :=
  fixesOff_firstReturn _ _

theorem fixesOff_faceReturn (Γ : Finset D) : FixesOff (R.faceReturn Γ) Γ :=
  fixesOff_firstReturn _ _

theorem fixesOff_psi (Γ : Finset D) : FixesOff (R.psi Γ) Γ :=
  (R.fixesOff_nodeReturn Γ).mul (R.fixesOff_faceReturn Γ)

/-- The skeleton of a set of corners: the hypermap on `D` with `node := a`, `face := b` and
`edge := (a * b)⁻¹`. Every dart outside `Γ` is a fixed point of all three. -/
noncomputable def skeleton (Γ : Finset D) : Hypermap D :=
  permMap (R.nodeReturn Γ) (R.faceReturn Γ)

/-- `Γ` is connected: any two elements of `Γ` lie in one component of the skeleton. -/
def SkeletonConnected (Γ : Finset D) : Prop := ∀ x ∈ Γ, ∀ y ∈ Γ, (R.skeleton Γ).gcomp x y

/-! ### Gluing and splitting -/

/-- The rotation system with the same reversal and the rotation `rot * ν`. -/
def glue (ν : Equiv.Perm D) : RotSystem D where
  rev := R.rev
  rev_rev := R.rev_rev
  rev_ne := R.rev_ne
  rot := R.rot * ν

/-- The split at `Γ`: the same reversal and the rotation `rot' := rot * a⁻¹`. For `d ∈ Γ`,
`rot' d = rot (a⁻¹ d)` closes the sector that ends at `d` on itself, and `rot' d = rot d` for
`d ∉ Γ`. The vertices of the split are the sectors. -/
noncomputable def split (Γ : Finset D) : RotSystem D := R.glue (R.nodeReturn Γ)⁻¹

theorem glue_facePerm (ν : Equiv.Perm D) : (R.glue ν).facePerm = ν⁻¹ * R.facePerm :=
  Equiv.ext fun _ => rfl

theorem split_rot (Γ : Finset D) : (R.split Γ).rot = R.rot * (R.nodeReturn Γ)⁻¹ := rfl

theorem split_rot_apply (Γ : Finset D) (x : D) :
    (R.split Γ).rot x = R.rot ((R.nodeReturn Γ)⁻¹ x) := rfl

theorem split_rot_of_not_mem {Γ : Finset D} {x : D} (hx : x ∉ Γ) :
    (R.split Γ).rot x = R.rot x := by
  rw [split_rot_apply, (R.fixesOff_nodeReturn Γ).inv x hx]

/-- The face permutation of the split is `a * face`. -/
theorem split_facePerm (Γ : Finset D) : (R.split Γ).facePerm = R.nodeReturn Γ * R.facePerm := by
  rw [split, glue_facePerm, inv_inv]

theorem nodeReturn_glue {ν : Equiv.Perm D} {S : Finset D} (hν : FixesOff ν S) :
    (R.glue ν).nodeReturn S = R.nodeReturn S * ν :=
  firstReturn_mul_right R.rot hν

theorem faceReturn_glue {ν : Equiv.Perm D} {S : Finset D} (hν : FixesOff ν S) :
    (R.glue ν).faceReturn S = ν⁻¹ * R.faceReturn S := by
  unfold faceReturn
  rw [glue_facePerm]
  exact firstReturn_mul_left _ hν.inv

/-- The rotation of the split has first return `1` to `Γ`: one corner of `Γ` per sector. -/
theorem nodeReturn_split (Γ : Finset D) : (R.split Γ).nodeReturn Γ = 1 := by
  rw [split, R.nodeReturn_glue (R.fixesOff_nodeReturn Γ).inv, mul_inv_cancel]

/-- The face permutation of the split has first return `ψ` to `Γ`. -/
theorem faceReturn_split (Γ : Finset D) : (R.split Γ).faceReturn Γ = R.psi Γ := by
  rw [split, R.faceReturn_glue (R.fixesOff_nodeReturn Γ).inv, inv_inv, psi]

/-- Splitting at a larger set forgets the smaller one. -/
theorem split_split {Γ₁ Γ₂ : Finset D} (h : Γ₁ ⊆ Γ₂) : (R.split Γ₁).split Γ₂ = R.split Γ₂ := by
  refine RotSystem.ext rfl ?_
  show (R.split Γ₁).rot * ((R.split Γ₁).nodeReturn Γ₂)⁻¹ = R.rot * (R.nodeReturn Γ₂)⁻¹
  have hν : FixesOff (R.nodeReturn Γ₁)⁻¹ Γ₂ := (R.fixesOff_nodeReturn Γ₁).inv.mono h
  rw [split, R.nodeReturn_glue hν]
  show R.rot * (R.nodeReturn Γ₁)⁻¹ * (R.nodeReturn Γ₂ * (R.nodeReturn Γ₁)⁻¹)⁻¹ =
    R.rot * (R.nodeReturn Γ₂)⁻¹
  rw [mul_inv_rev, inv_inv, mul_assoc, inv_mul_cancel_left]

/-- Gluing the split with `a` gives back the rotation system. -/
theorem glue_split (Γ : Finset D) : (R.split Γ).glue (R.nodeReturn Γ) = R := by
  refine RotSystem.ext rfl ?_
  exact inv_mul_cancel_right R.rot (R.nodeReturn Γ)

/-- A map with one marked corner per vertex is the split of each of its gluings. -/
theorem split_glue {Γ : Finset D} (h1 : R.nodeReturn Γ = 1) {ν : Equiv.Perm D}
    (hν : FixesOff ν Γ) : (R.glue ν).split Γ = R := by
  refine RotSystem.ext rfl ?_
  show R.rot * ν * ((R.glue ν).nodeReturn Γ)⁻¹ = R.rot
  rw [R.nodeReturn_glue hν, h1, one_mul, mul_inv_cancel_right]

/-! ### The identity -/

theorem orb_split_rot (Γ : Finset D) :
    orb (R.split Γ).rot + orb (R.nodeReturn Γ) = orb R.rot + Fintype.card D := by
  have h := orb_mul_right R.rot (R.fixesOff_nodeReturn Γ).inv
  rw [show firstReturn R.rot Γ * (R.nodeReturn Γ)⁻¹ = 1 from mul_inv_cancel _, orb_one] at h
  exact h

theorem orb_split_face (Γ : Finset D) :
    orb (R.split Γ).facePerm + orb (R.faceReturn Γ) = orb R.facePerm + orb (R.psi Γ) := by
  rw [split_facePerm]
  exact orb_mul_left R.facePerm (R.fixesOff_nodeReturn Γ)

/-- **The genus of a split.** With `P := R.split Γ`, for every `Γ`:
`g(R) + C(P) + Cˢ = g(P) + g(skeleton) + C(R) + orb ψ`, where the skeleton and `ψ` are counted on
all of `D`. -/
theorem genus_split (Γ : Finset D) :
    R.toHypermap.genus + (R.split Γ).numComponents + nComp (R.skeleton Γ).glink Set.univ =
      (R.split Γ).toHypermap.genus + (R.skeleton Γ).genus + R.numComponents + orb (R.psi Γ) := by
  have hR := R.toHypermap.evenGenus
  have hP := (R.split Γ).toHypermap.evenGenus
  have hS := (R.skeleton Γ).evenGenus
  unfold Hypermap.EvenGenus Hypermap.eulerLhs Hypermap.eulerRhs at hR hP hS
  have hnode : fcard (R.split Γ).toHypermap.node Set.univ +
      fcard (R.skeleton Γ).node Set.univ =
      fcard R.toHypermap.node Set.univ + Fintype.card D := R.orb_split_rot Γ
  have hface : fcard (R.split Γ).toHypermap.face Set.univ +
      fcard (R.skeleton Γ).face Set.univ =
      fcard R.toHypermap.face Set.univ + orb (R.psi Γ) := R.orb_split_face Γ
  have hE : fcard (R.split Γ).toHypermap.edge Set.univ = fcard R.toHypermap.edge Set.univ := rfl
  have hSE : fcard (R.skeleton Γ).edge Set.univ = orb (R.psi Γ) := orb_inv (R.psi Γ)
  unfold numComponents
  omega

/-! ### The tiles -/

/-- Forward closure under `rev` and `rot` is closure under the components. -/
theorem mem_of_gcomp {A : Set D} (hrev : ∀ x ∈ A, R.rev x ∈ A) (hrot : ∀ x ∈ A, R.rot x ∈ A)
    {x y : D} (h : R.toHypermap.gcomp x y) (hx : x ∈ A) : y ∈ A := by
  have hsym : ∀ z ∈ A, R.rot.symm z ∈ A := fun z hz => by
    have h1 : fconnect R.rot (R.rot.symm z) z := by
      have h2 := fconnect1 (⇑R.rot) (R.rot.symm z)
      rwa [Equiv.apply_symm_apply] at h2
    refine mem_of_connect_of_forward ?_ (fconnect_sym R.rot.injective _ _ h1) hz
    rintro u _ rfl hu
    exact hrot u hu
  refine mem_of_connect_of_forward ?_ h hx
  rintro u _ (rfl | rfl | rfl) hu
  · exact hrev u hu
  · exact hrot u hu
  · exact hsym _ (hrev u hu)

/-- A link of a tile: along an edge, or along the rotation from a dart outside `Γ`. -/
def TileLink (Γ : Finset D) (u v : D) : Prop := v = R.rev u ∨ (u ∉ Γ ∧ v = R.rot u)

private theorem eqvGen_of_trail {Γ : Finset D} {y z : D} (h : Trail R.rot Γ y z) :
    Relation.EqvGen (R.TileLink Γ) y z := by
  induction h with
  | here _ => exact Relation.EqvGen.refl _
  | step hn _ ih =>
    exact Relation.EqvGen.trans _ _ _ (Relation.EqvGen.rel _ _ (Or.inr ⟨hn, rfl⟩)) ih

/-- **The tiles.** The components of the split are the classes of the equivalence relation
generated by `v = rev u` and `u ∉ Γ ∧ v = rot u`. -/
theorem gcomp_split_iff (Γ : Finset D) (x y : D) :
    (R.split Γ).toHypermap.gcomp x y ↔ Relation.EqvGen (R.TileLink Γ) x y := by
  constructor
  · intro h
    refine (R.split Γ).mem_of_gcomp (A := {z | Relation.EqvGen (R.TileLink Γ) x z}) ?_ ?_ h
      (Relation.EqvGen.refl x)
    · intro z hz
      exact Relation.EqvGen.trans _ _ _ hz (Relation.EqvGen.rel _ _ (Or.inl rfl))
    · intro z hz
      by_cases hzΓ : z ∈ Γ
      · have hw : (R.nodeReturn Γ)⁻¹ z ∈ Γ := ((R.fixesOff_nodeReturn Γ).inv.mem_iff z).2 hzΓ
        have ht := firstReturn_trail R.rot hw
        have hz' : firstReturn R.rot Γ ((R.nodeReturn Γ)⁻¹ z) = z :=
          (R.nodeReturn Γ).apply_symm_apply z
        rw [hz'] at ht
        exact Relation.EqvGen.trans _ _ _ hz (Relation.EqvGen.symm _ _ (R.eqvGen_of_trail ht))
      · have hrot : (R.split Γ).rot z = R.rot z := R.split_rot_of_not_mem hzΓ
        show Relation.EqvGen (R.TileLink Γ) x ((R.split Γ).rot z)
        rw [hrot]
        exact Relation.EqvGen.trans _ _ _ hz (Relation.EqvGen.rel _ _ (Or.inr ⟨hzΓ, rfl⟩))
  · intro h
    induction h with
    | rel a b hab =>
      rcases hab with rfl | ⟨ha, rfl⟩
      · exact connect_of_rel (Or.inl rfl)
      · exact connect_of_rel (Or.inr (Or.inl (R.split_rot_of_not_mem ha)))
    | refl a => exact connect_refl a
    | symm a b _ ih => exact (R.split Γ).toHypermap.glinkC _ _ ih
    | trans a b c _ _ ih1 ih2 => exact connect_trans ih1 ih2

private theorem gcomp_of_eqvGen {Γ : Finset D} {x y : D}
    (h : Relation.EqvGen (R.TileLink Γ) x y) : R.toHypermap.gcomp x y := by
  induction h with
  | rel a b hab =>
    rcases hab with rfl | ⟨-, rfl⟩
    · exact connect_of_rel (Or.inl rfl)
    · exact connect_of_rel (Or.inr (Or.inl rfl))
  | refl a => exact connect_refl a
  | symm a b _ ih => exact R.toHypermap.glinkC _ _ ih
  | trans a b c _ _ ih1 ih2 => exact connect_trans ih1 ih2

/-- A component of the split lies in a component of the rotation system. -/
theorem gcomp_of_gcomp_split {Γ : Finset D} {x y : D} (h : (R.split Γ).toHypermap.gcomp x y) :
    R.toHypermap.gcomp x y :=
  R.gcomp_of_eqvGen ((R.gcomp_split_iff Γ x y).1 h)

/-- A component of the skeleton lies in a component of the rotation system. -/
theorem gcomp_of_gcomp_skeleton {Γ : Finset D} {x y : D} (h : (R.skeleton Γ).gcomp x y) :
    R.toHypermap.gcomp x y := by
  have hn : ∀ u, R.toHypermap.gcomp u (R.nodeReturn Γ u) := fun u =>
    R.toHypermap.gcomp_of_cnode (fconnect_firstReturn R.rot Γ u)
  have hf : ∀ u, R.toHypermap.gcomp u (R.faceReturn Γ u) := fun u =>
    R.toHypermap.gcomp_of_cface (fconnect_firstReturn R.facePerm Γ u)
  refine connect_sub (fun u v huv => ?_) h
  rcases huv with rfl | rfl | rfl
  · have hv : R.nodeReturn Γ (R.faceReturn Γ ((R.psi Γ)⁻¹ u)) = u :=
      (R.psi Γ).apply_symm_apply u
    have h1 := connect_trans (hf ((R.psi Γ)⁻¹ u)) (hn _)
    rw [hv] at h1
    exact R.toHypermap.glinkC _ _ h1
  · exact hn u
  · exact hf u

/-- Two corners of `Γ` are adjacent if they lie at one vertex or on one face. This is the line
graph of the bipartite graph between vertices and faces with one edge per corner of `Γ`. -/
def CornerLink (Γ : Finset D) (u v : D) : Prop :=
  u ∈ Γ ∧ v ∈ Γ ∧ (R.toHypermap.cnode u v ∨ R.toHypermap.cface u v)

/-- From a corner of `Γ`, the component of the skeleton is the component of the corner graph. So
`SkeletonConnected` says that the bipartite graph between vertices and faces with one edge per
corner of `Γ` is connected, apart from vertices and faces without such an edge. -/
theorem gcomp_skeleton_iff {Γ : Finset D} {x y : D} (hx : x ∈ Γ) :
    (R.skeleton Γ).gcomp x y ↔ connect (R.CornerLink Γ) x y := by
  constructor
  · intro h
    have key : y ∈ Γ ∧ connect (R.CornerLink Γ) x y := by
      induction h with
      | refl => exact ⟨hx, connect_refl x⟩
      | @tail u v _ huv ih =>
        obtain ⟨hu, hxu⟩ := ih
        rcases huv with rfl | rfl | rfl
        · have hw : (R.psi Γ)⁻¹ u ∈ Γ := ((R.fixesOff_psi Γ).inv.mem_iff u).2 hu
          have hb := ((R.fixesOff_faceReturn Γ).mem_iff _).2 hw
          have hab : firstReturn R.rot Γ (R.faceReturn Γ ((R.psi Γ)⁻¹ u)) = u :=
            (R.psi Γ).apply_symm_apply u
          have h1 := fconnect_firstReturn R.rot Γ (R.faceReturn Γ ((R.psi Γ)⁻¹ u))
          rw [hab] at h1
          have h2 := fconnect_firstReturn R.facePerm Γ ((R.psi Γ)⁻¹ u)
          exact ⟨hw, connect_trans hxu (connect_trans
            (connect_of_rel ⟨hu, hb, Or.inl (R.toHypermap.cnodeC.1 h1)⟩)
            (connect_of_rel ⟨hb, hw, Or.inr (R.toHypermap.cfaceC.1 h2)⟩))⟩
        · have hv := ((R.fixesOff_nodeReturn Γ).mem_iff u).2 hu
          exact ⟨hv, connect_trans hxu
            (connect_of_rel ⟨hu, hv, Or.inl (fconnect_firstReturn R.rot Γ u)⟩)⟩
        · have hv := ((R.fixesOff_faceReturn Γ).mem_iff u).2 hu
          exact ⟨hv, connect_trans hxu
            (connect_of_rel ⟨hu, hv, Or.inr (fconnect_firstReturn R.facePerm Γ u)⟩)⟩
    exact key.2
  · refine connect_sub ?_
    rintro u v ⟨hu, hv, h | h⟩
    · have h' : fconnect (R.nodeReturn Γ) u v := (fconnect_firstReturn_iff R.rot hu hv).2 h
      exact (R.skeleton Γ).gcomp_of_cnode h'
    · have h' : fconnect (R.faceReturn Γ) u v := (fconnect_firstReturn_iff R.facePerm hu hv).2 h
      exact (R.skeleton Γ).gcomp_of_cface h'

/-- An orbit of the first return of the face permutation lies in one component. -/
theorem gcomp_of_fconnect_faceReturn {Γ : Finset D} {x y : D}
    (h : fconnect (R.faceReturn Γ) x y) : R.toHypermap.gcomp x y :=
  R.toHypermap.gcomp_of_cface (fconnect_of_fconnect_firstReturn h)

/-- A `ψ`-orbit lies in one component of the split. -/
theorem gcomp_split_of_fconnect_psi {Γ : Finset D} {x y : D} (h : fconnect (R.psi Γ) x y) :
    (R.split Γ).toHypermap.gcomp x y := by
  rw [← faceReturn_split] at h
  exact (R.split Γ).gcomp_of_fconnect_faceReturn h

/-! ### The disks -/

/-- Every component of the split of a connected rotation system at a nonempty set contains an
element of the set: a component with none would be closed under `rev` and `rot`, so it would be
everything. -/
theorem split_meets (hc : R.Connected) {Γ : Finset D} (hΓ : Γ.Nonempty) (x : D) :
    ∃ y ∈ Γ, (R.split Γ).toHypermap.gcomp x y := by
  by_contra hn
  obtain ⟨z, hz⟩ := hΓ
  have hxz : R.toHypermap.gcomp x z :=
    connect_of_nComp_eq_one R.toHypermap.glinkC hc (Set.mem_univ x) (Set.mem_univ z)
  have hA : z ∈ {w | ∀ y ∈ Γ, ¬ (R.split Γ).toHypermap.gcomp w y} := by
    refine R.mem_of_gcomp ?_ ?_ hxz fun y hy h => hn ⟨y, hy, h⟩
    · intro w hw y hy h
      exact hw y hy (connect_trans (connect_of_rel (Or.inl rfl)) h)
    · intro w hw y hy h
      have hwΓ : w ∉ Γ := fun hm => hw w hm (connect_refl w)
      exact hw y hy (connect_trans
        (connect_of_rel (Or.inr (Or.inl (R.split_rot_of_not_mem hwΓ)))) h)
  exact hA z hz (connect_refl z)

/-- The components of the skeleton of a connected set: one for `Γ`, and one per dart outside. -/
theorem nComp_skeleton {Γ : Finset D} (hΓ : Γ.Nonempty) (hS : R.SkeletonConnected Γ) :
    nComp (R.skeleton Γ).glink Set.univ = 1 + Γᶜ.card := by
  rw [show nComp (R.skeleton Γ).glink Set.univ = _ from
    permMap_nComp (R.fixesOff_nodeReturn Γ) (R.fixesOff_faceReturn Γ),
    show nComp (permMap (R.nodeReturn Γ) (R.faceReturn Γ)).glink (Γ : Set D) = 1 from
      nComp_eq_one_of_connect (R.skeleton Γ).glinkC hΓ hS]

/-- **The disks.** The split of a planar connected rotation system at a nonempty connected set of
corners is planar, its skeleton is planar, every component of the split meets `Γ`, and each of them
contains exactly one `ψ`-orbit of `Γ`. -/
theorem split_planar (hR : R.Planar) (hc : R.Connected) {Γ : Finset D} (hΓ : Γ.Nonempty)
    (hS : R.SkeletonConnected Γ) :
    (R.split Γ).Planar ∧ (R.skeleton Γ).Planar ∧
      (∀ x, ∃ y ∈ Γ, (R.split Γ).toHypermap.gcomp x y) ∧
      ∀ x ∈ Γ, ∀ y ∈ Γ, ((R.split Γ).toHypermap.gcomp x y ↔ fconnect (R.psi Γ) x y) := by
  have hmeet := R.split_meets hc hΓ
  have hgs := (R.split Γ).toHypermap.glinkC
  have himp : ∀ x y, fconnect (R.psi Γ) x y → (R.split Γ).toHypermap.gcomp x y :=
    fun _ _ h => R.gcomp_split_of_fconnect_psi h
  have hP : (R.split Γ).numComponents = nComp (R.split Γ).toHypermap.glink (Γ : Set D) :=
    nComp_univ_of_meets hgs hmeet
  have hle : nComp (R.split Γ).toHypermap.glink (Γ : Set D) ≤ fcard (R.psi Γ) (Γ : Set D) :=
    nComp_le_of_imp himp _
  have hid := R.genus_split Γ
  have hCs := R.nComp_skeleton hΓ hS
  have hψ := orb_eq_add_card (R.fixesOff_psi Γ)
  have hg0 : R.toHypermap.genus = 0 := hR
  have hC1 : R.numComponents = 1 := hc
  have hgP : (R.split Γ).toHypermap.genus = 0 := by omega
  have hgS : (R.skeleton Γ).genus = 0 := by omega
  have heq : nComp (R.split Γ).toHypermap.glink (Γ : Set D) = fcard (R.psi Γ) (Γ : Set D) := by
    omega
  refine ⟨hgP, hgS, hmeet, fun x hx y hy => ⟨fun h => ?_, himp x y⟩⟩
  exact connect_of_nComp_eq (fconnect_sym (R.psi Γ).injective) hgs himp heq hx hy h

/-! ### Replacing the disks -/

/-- A planar map with marked corners, such that every vertex has at most one marked corner, every
component has a marked corner, and the first return of the face permutation has exactly one orbit
of marked corners per component. -/
structure IsDisks (Γ : Finset D) : Prop where
  /-- The map is planar. -/
  planar : R.Planar
  /-- At most one marked corner per vertex. -/
  node_return : R.nodeReturn Γ = 1
  /-- Every component has a marked corner. -/
  meets : ∀ x, ∃ y ∈ Γ, R.toHypermap.gcomp x y
  /-- Marked corners in one component lie in one orbit of the first return. -/
  one_orbit : ∀ x ∈ Γ, ∀ y ∈ Γ, R.toHypermap.gcomp x y → fconnect (R.faceReturn Γ) x y

variable {R} in
/-- A map of disks has as many components as the first return of its faces has orbits of marked
corners. -/
theorem IsDisks.numComponents_eq {Γ : Finset D} (hR : R.IsDisks Γ) :
    R.numComponents = fcard (R.faceReturn Γ) (Γ : Set D) :=
  (nComp_univ_of_meets R.toHypermap.glinkC hR.meets).trans
    (ncard_image_eq_of_ker _ _ fun x hx y hy => by
      rw [comp_eq_iff R.toHypermap.glinkC, comp_eq_iff (fconnect_sym (R.faceReturn Γ).injective)]
      exact ⟨hR.one_orbit x hx y hy, R.gcomp_of_fconnect_faceReturn⟩)

/-- The split of a planar connected rotation system at a nonempty connected set of corners consists
of disks. -/
theorem split_isDisks (hR : R.Planar) (hc : R.Connected) {Γ : Finset D} (hΓ : Γ.Nonempty)
    (hS : R.SkeletonConnected Γ) : (R.split Γ).IsDisks Γ := by
  obtain ⟨hp, -, hm, ho⟩ := R.split_planar hR hc hΓ hS
  refine ⟨hp, R.nodeReturn_split Γ, hm, fun x hx y hy h => ?_⟩
  rw [faceReturn_split]
  exact (ho x hx y hy).1 h

/-- For a nonempty connected set of corners of a planar connected rotation system, the split has as
many components as `ψ` has orbits in `Γ`. -/
theorem numComponents_split (hR : R.Planar) (hc : R.Connected) {Γ : Finset D} (hΓ : Γ.Nonempty)
    (hS : R.SkeletonConnected Γ) : (R.split Γ).numComponents = fcard (R.psi Γ) (Γ : Set D) := by
  rw [(R.split_isDisks hR hc hΓ hS).numComponents_eq, faceReturn_split]

variable {R}

theorem nodeReturn_glue_of_one {Γ : Finset D} (h1 : R.nodeReturn Γ = 1) {ν : Equiv.Perm D}
    (hν : FixesOff ν Γ) : (R.glue ν).nodeReturn Γ = ν := by
  rw [R.nodeReturn_glue hν, h1, one_mul]

theorem skeleton_glue {Γ : Finset D} (h1 : R.nodeReturn Γ = 1) {ν : Equiv.Perm D}
    (hν : FixesOff ν Γ) : (R.glue ν).skeleton Γ = permMap ν (ν⁻¹ * R.faceReturn Γ) := by
  rw [skeleton, nodeReturn_glue_of_one h1 hν, R.faceReturn_glue hν]

theorem psi_glue {Γ : Finset D} (h1 : R.nodeReturn Γ = 1) {ν : Equiv.Perm D}
    (hν : FixesOff ν Γ) : (R.glue ν).psi Γ = R.faceReturn Γ := by
  rw [psi, nodeReturn_glue_of_one h1 hν, R.faceReturn_glue hν, mul_inv_cancel_left]

/-- A map whose components all have a marked corner, glued along `ν`, is connected if the skeleton
connects the marked corners. -/
theorem glue_connected {Γ : Finset D} (h1 : R.nodeReturn Γ = 1)
    (hm : ∀ x, ∃ y ∈ Γ, R.toHypermap.gcomp x y) (hΓ : Γ.Nonempty) {ν : Equiv.Perm D}
    (hν : FixesOff ν Γ)
    (hconn : ∀ x ∈ Γ, ∀ y ∈ Γ, (permMap ν (ν⁻¹ * R.faceReturn Γ)).gcomp x y) :
    (R.glue ν).Connected := by
  have hsplit := R.split_glue h1 hν
  have hup : ∀ {x y : D}, R.toHypermap.gcomp x y → (R.glue ν).toHypermap.gcomp x y := by
    intro x y h
    rw [← hsplit] at h
    exact (R.glue ν).gcomp_of_gcomp_split h
  have hskel : ∀ x ∈ Γ, ∀ y ∈ Γ, (R.glue ν).toHypermap.gcomp x y := fun x hx y hy =>
    (R.glue ν).gcomp_of_gcomp_skeleton (Γ := Γ) (by rw [skeleton_glue h1 hν]; exact hconn x hx y hy)
  have hsym := (R.glue ν).toHypermap.glinkC
  obtain ⟨z, hz⟩ := hΓ
  refine nComp_eq_one_of_connect hsym ⟨z, Set.mem_univ z⟩ fun x _ y _ => ?_
  obtain ⟨cx, hcx, hx⟩ := hm x
  obtain ⟨cy, hcy, hy⟩ := hm y
  exact connect_trans (hup hx) (connect_trans (hskel cx hcx cy hcy) (hsym _ _ (hup hy)))

/-- **The replacement lemma.** A map of disks glued along a permutation `ν` of its marked corners is
planar and connected, with first returns `ν` and `ν⁻¹ * ψ'`, if the skeleton with node `ν` and face
`ν⁻¹ * ψ'` is connected on the marked corners and planar. -/
theorem glue_planar {Γ : Finset D} (hR : R.IsDisks Γ) (hΓ : Γ.Nonempty) {ν : Equiv.Perm D}
    (hν : FixesOff ν Γ)
    (hconn : ∀ x ∈ Γ, ∀ y ∈ Γ, (permMap ν (ν⁻¹ * R.faceReturn Γ)).gcomp x y)
    (hplanar : (permMap ν (ν⁻¹ * R.faceReturn Γ)).Planar) :
    (R.glue ν).Planar ∧ (R.glue ν).Connected ∧ (R.glue ν).nodeReturn Γ = ν ∧
      (R.glue ν).faceReturn Γ = ν⁻¹ * R.faceReturn Γ := by
  have hQ := glue_connected hR.node_return hR.meets hΓ hν hconn
  have hid := (R.glue ν).genus_split Γ
  rw [R.split_glue hR.node_return hν, skeleton_glue hR.node_return hν,
    psi_glue hR.node_return hν] at hid
  have hP := hR.numComponents_eq
  have hCs : nComp (permMap ν (ν⁻¹ * R.faceReturn Γ)).glink Set.univ = 1 + Γᶜ.card := by
    rw [permMap_nComp hν (hν.inv.mul (R.fixesOff_faceReturn Γ)),
      nComp_eq_one_of_connect (permMap _ _).glinkC hΓ hconn]
  have hψ := orb_eq_add_card (R.fixesOff_faceReturn Γ)
  have hgP : R.toHypermap.genus = 0 := hR.planar
  have hgS : (permMap ν (ν⁻¹ * R.faceReturn Γ)).genus = 0 := hplanar
  have hC1 : (R.glue ν).numComponents = 1 := hQ
  refine ⟨?_, hQ, nodeReturn_glue_of_one hR.node_return hν, R.faceReturn_glue hν⟩
  show (R.glue ν).toHypermap.genus = 0
  omega

variable (R)

section Replace

variable {D' : Type*} [Fintype D'] [DecidableEq D']

/-- **The replacement lemma, along a bijection.** Let `R` be planar and connected, `Γ` nonempty and
connected, and let `P'` be a map of disks with marked corners `Γ'`. If `β : Γ' ≃ Γ` carries the
first return `ψ'` of the faces of `P'` to `ψ` and `ν'` to `a`, then `P'.glue ν'` is planar and
connected, with first returns `ν'` and `ν'⁻¹ * ψ'`, which `β` carries to `a` and `b`. -/
theorem glue_planar_of_conjVia (hR : R.Planar) (hc : R.Connected) {Γ : Finset D} (hΓ : Γ.Nonempty)
    (hS : R.SkeletonConnected Γ) {P' : RotSystem D'} {Γ' : Finset D'} (hP' : P'.IsDisks Γ')
    (β : Γ' ≃ Γ) {ν' : Equiv.Perm D'} (hν' : FixesOff ν' Γ')
    (hνa : ConjVia β ν' (R.nodeReturn Γ)) (hψ : ConjVia β (P'.faceReturn Γ') (R.psi Γ)) :
    (P'.glue ν').Planar ∧ (P'.glue ν').Connected ∧ (P'.glue ν').nodeReturn Γ' = ν' ∧
      (P'.glue ν').faceReturn Γ' = ν'⁻¹ * P'.faceReturn Γ' ∧
      ConjVia β ((P'.glue ν').nodeReturn Γ') (R.nodeReturn Γ) ∧
      ConjVia β ((P'.glue ν').faceReturn Γ') (R.faceReturn Γ) := by
  have hb : ConjVia β (ν'⁻¹ * P'.faceReturn Γ') (R.faceReturn Γ) := by
    have h := hνa.inv.mul hψ
    rwa [psi, inv_mul_cancel_left] at h
  have hfix : FixesOff (ν'⁻¹ * P'.faceReturn Γ') Γ' := hν'.inv.mul (P'.fixesOff_faceReturn Γ')
  have hΓ' : Γ'.Nonempty := by
    obtain ⟨z, hz⟩ := hΓ
    exact ⟨_, (β.symm ⟨z, hz⟩).2⟩
  have hconn : ∀ x ∈ Γ', ∀ y ∈ Γ', (permMap ν' (ν'⁻¹ * P'.faceReturn Γ')).gcomp x y :=
    fun x hx y hy => (permMap_gcomp_corr hνa hb ⟨hx, rfl⟩ ⟨hy, rfl⟩).2
      (hS _ (β ⟨x, hx⟩).2 _ (β ⟨y, hy⟩).2)
  have hplanar : (permMap ν' (ν'⁻¹ * P'.faceReturn Γ')).Planar := by
    show (permMap ν' (ν'⁻¹ * P'.faceReturn Γ')).genus = 0
    rw [permMap_genus_eq β hν' hfix (R.fixesOff_nodeReturn Γ) (R.fixesOff_faceReturn Γ) hνa hb]
    exact (R.split_planar hR hc hΓ hS).2.1
  obtain ⟨h1, h2, h3, h4⟩ := glue_planar hP' hΓ' hν' hconn hplanar
  exact ⟨h1, h2, h3, h4, by rw [h3]; exact hνa, by rw [h4]; exact hb⟩

/-- The disks `P'` glued along the rotation of `R` at `Γ`, through `β`. -/
noncomputable def replace (Γ : Finset D) (P' : RotSystem D') {Γ' : Finset D'} (β : Γ' ≃ Γ) :
    RotSystem D' :=
  P'.glue (transport β (R.nodeReturn Γ) (R.fixesOff_nodeReturn Γ).mem_iff)

/-- **Replacement.** Replacing the components of a split by any disks with the same cyclic order of
marked corners keeps planarity and connectivity, and the first returns are carried over from `a`
and `b`, because the skeleton does not change. -/
theorem replace_planar (hR : R.Planar) (hc : R.Connected) {Γ : Finset D} (hΓ : Γ.Nonempty)
    (hS : R.SkeletonConnected Γ) {P' : RotSystem D'} {Γ' : Finset D'} (hP' : P'.IsDisks Γ')
    (β : Γ' ≃ Γ) (hψ : ConjVia β (P'.faceReturn Γ') (R.psi Γ)) :
    (R.replace Γ P' β).Planar ∧ (R.replace Γ P' β).Connected ∧
      (R.replace Γ P' β).nodeReturn Γ' =
        transport β (R.nodeReturn Γ) (R.fixesOff_nodeReturn Γ).mem_iff ∧
      (R.replace Γ P' β).faceReturn Γ' =
        transport β (R.faceReturn Γ) (R.fixesOff_faceReturn Γ).mem_iff := by
  obtain ⟨h1, h2, h3, -, -, h6⟩ := R.glue_planar_of_conjVia hR hc hΓ hS hP' β
    (fixesOff_transport β _ _) (conjVia_transport β _ _) hψ
  exact ⟨h1, h2, h3, eq_transport _ ((R.replace Γ P' β).fixesOff_faceReturn Γ') h6⟩

/-- The split of a replacement at the marked corners is the map of disks. -/
theorem split_replace (Γ : Finset D) {P' : RotSystem D'} {Γ' : Finset D'} (hP' : P'.IsDisks Γ')
    (β : Γ' ≃ Γ) : (R.replace Γ P' β).split Γ' = P' :=
  P'.split_glue hP'.node_return (fixesOff_transport β _ _)

/-- Replacing the components of a split by themselves gives back the rotation system. -/
theorem replace_split (Γ : Finset D) : R.replace Γ (R.split Γ) (Equiv.refl Γ) = R := by
  have h : transport (Equiv.refl Γ) (R.nodeReturn Γ) (R.fixesOff_nodeReturn Γ).mem_iff =
      R.nodeReturn Γ :=
    (eq_transport _ (R.fixesOff_nodeReturn Γ)
      (conjVia_refl (R.fixesOff_nodeReturn Γ).mem_iff)).symm
  unfold replace
  rw [h]
  exact R.glue_split Γ

end Replace

/-! ### An instance -/

section Instance

/-- Two corners of `triangle`, both at the vertex `a` and both on its inner face. -/
def triangleCorners : Finset (Fin 10) := {0, 6}

private theorem triangle_rot_values :
    triangle.rot 0 = 6 ∧ triangle.rot 6 = 5 ∧ triangle.rot 5 = 8 ∧ triangle.rot 8 = 0 := by
  decide

private theorem triangle_face_values :
    triangle.facePerm 0 = 2 ∧ triangle.facePerm 2 = 4 ∧ triangle.facePerm 4 = 6 ∧
      triangle.facePerm 6 = 7 ∧ triangle.facePerm 7 = 0 := by
  decide

/-- The first return of the rotation exchanges the two corners. -/
theorem triangle_nodeReturn : triangle.nodeReturn triangleCorners 0 = 6 ∧
    triangle.nodeReturn triangleCorners 6 = 0 := by
  obtain ⟨h0, h6, h5, h8⟩ := triangle_rot_values
  constructor
  · refine firstReturn_eq_of_trail _ (by decide) ?_
    rw [h0]
    exact Trail.here (by decide)
  · refine firstReturn_eq_of_trail _ (by decide) ?_
    rw [h6]
    refine Trail.step (by decide) ?_
    rw [h5]
    refine Trail.step (by decide) ?_
    rw [h8]
    exact Trail.here (by decide)

/-- The first return of the face permutation exchanges the two corners too. -/
theorem triangle_faceReturn : triangle.faceReturn triangleCorners 0 = 6 ∧
    triangle.faceReturn triangleCorners 6 = 0 := by
  obtain ⟨h0, h2, h4, h6, h7⟩ := triangle_face_values
  constructor
  · refine firstReturn_eq_of_trail _ (by decide) ?_
    rw [h0]
    refine Trail.step (by decide) ?_
    rw [h2]
    refine Trail.step (by decide) ?_
    rw [h4]
    exact Trail.here (by decide)
  · refine firstReturn_eq_of_trail _ (by decide) ?_
    rw [h6]
    refine Trail.step (by decide) ?_
    rw [h7]
    exact Trail.here (by decide)

/-- So `ψ` fixes both corners. -/
theorem triangle_psi : triangle.psi triangleCorners 0 = 0 ∧
    triangle.psi triangleCorners 6 = 6 := by
  constructor
  · show triangle.nodeReturn triangleCorners (triangle.faceReturn triangleCorners 0) = 0
    rw [triangle_faceReturn.1, triangle_nodeReturn.2]
  · show triangle.nodeReturn triangleCorners (triangle.faceReturn triangleCorners 6) = 6
    rw [triangle_faceReturn.2, triangle_nodeReturn.1]

theorem triangleCorners_nonempty : triangleCorners.Nonempty := ⟨0, by decide⟩

/-- The two corners are connected in the skeleton. -/
theorem triangle_skeletonConnected : triangle.SkeletonConnected triangleCorners := by
  have h06 : (triangle.skeleton triangleCorners).gcomp 0 6 :=
    connect_of_rel (Or.inr (Or.inl triangle_nodeReturn.1))
  have h60 : (triangle.skeleton triangleCorners).gcomp 6 0 :=
    connect_of_rel (Or.inr (Or.inl triangle_nodeReturn.2))
  have hmem : ∀ x : Fin 10, x ∈ triangleCorners → x = 0 ∨ x = 6 := by decide
  intro x hx y hy
  rcases hmem x hx with rfl | rfl <;> rcases hmem y hy with rfl | rfl
  · exact connect_refl _
  · exact h06
  · exact h60
  · exact connect_refl _

/-- The hypotheses of `split_planar` hold for `triangle` at the two corners, so its conclusions
hold there. -/
theorem triangle_split_planar :
    (triangle.split triangleCorners).Planar ∧ (triangle.skeleton triangleCorners).Planar ∧
      (∀ x, ∃ y ∈ triangleCorners, (triangle.split triangleCorners).toHypermap.gcomp x y) ∧
      ∀ x ∈ triangleCorners, ∀ y ∈ triangleCorners,
        ((triangle.split triangleCorners).toHypermap.gcomp x y ↔
          fconnect (triangle.psi triangleCorners) x y) :=
  triangle.split_planar triangle_planar triangle_connected triangleCorners_nonempty
    triangle_skeletonConnected

private theorem triangle_not_fconnect_psi : ¬ fconnect (triangle.psi triangleCorners) 0 6 := by
  intro h
  obtain ⟨n, hn⟩ := fconnect_iff_iterate.1 h
  rw [Function.iterate_fixed triangle_psi.1 n] at hn
  exact absurd hn (by decide)

/-- The split has exactly two tiles: the two corners lie in different components, as `ψ` fixes both,
and every component meets the two corners. The pendant edge at `p` comes off the rest. -/
theorem triangle_split_two_tiles :
    ¬ (triangle.split triangleCorners).toHypermap.gcomp 0 6 ∧
      (triangle.split triangleCorners).numComponents = 2 := by
  refine ⟨fun h => triangle_not_fconnect_psi
    ((triangle_split_planar.2.2.2 0 (by decide) 6 (by decide)).1 h), ?_⟩
  rw [triangle.numComponents_split triangle_planar triangle_connected triangleCorners_nonempty
    triangle_skeletonConnected]
  have hne : comp (frel (triangle.psi triangleCorners)) 0 ≠
      comp (frel (triangle.psi triangleCorners)) 6 := fun h => triangle_not_fconnect_psi
    ((comp_eq_iff (fconnect_sym (triangle.psi triangleCorners).injective)).1 h)
  have hset : ((triangleCorners : Finset (Fin 10)) : Set (Fin 10)) = {0, 6} := by
    simp [triangleCorners]
  rw [hset]
  show (comp _ '' ({0, 6} : Set (Fin 10))).ncard = 2
  rw [Set.image_pair, Set.ncard_pair hne]

/-- The split of `triangle` consists of disks, it meets the hypotheses of `replace_planar` under the
identity of the two corners, and replacing the disks by themselves gives `triangle` back. -/
theorem triangle_replace : (triangle.split triangleCorners).IsDisks triangleCorners ∧
    ConjVia (Equiv.refl triangleCorners)
      ((triangle.split triangleCorners).faceReturn triangleCorners)
      (triangle.psi triangleCorners) ∧
    triangle.replace triangleCorners (triangle.split triangleCorners)
      (Equiv.refl triangleCorners) = triangle := by
  refine ⟨triangle.split_isDisks triangle_planar triangle_connected triangleCorners_nonempty
    triangle_skeletonConnected, ?_, triangle.replace_split triangleCorners⟩
  rw [faceReturn_split]
  exact conjVia_refl (triangle.fixesOff_psi triangleCorners).mem_iff

end Instance

